.TH RLOCATE-UPDATEDB 1 "2026-10-20" "rlocate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rlocate-updatedb \- build an rlocate file-name index
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rlocate-updatedb
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIROOT\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rlocate-updatedb
walks one or more directory trees and builds the trigram index queried by
.BR rlocate (1).
If no \fIROOT\fR is given, the filesystem root
.RB ( / )
is indexed.
.PP
The walk does not follow symbolic links. It crosses mount boundaries by
default, skipping filesystems whose type is network or pseudo (for example
.BR nfs ", " smbfs ", " devfs ", " proc ).
Directory names such as
.B .git
and absolute paths such as
.B /tmp
(and, on macOS, the APFS
.B /System/Volumes/Data
firmlink and
.BR /Volumes )
are pruned by default.
.PP
The index is written to a temporary file and installed atomically. When built
as root it is made world-readable so any user can query it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIPATH\fR"
Write the index to \fIPATH\fR instead of the platform default.
.TP
.BR \-\-conf " \fIFILE\fR"
Read extra prune rules from an \fBupdatedb.conf\fR-style file
.RB ( PRUNEPATHS ", " PRUNENAMES ", " PRUNEFS ).
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-one\-file\-system
Do not descend into other mounted filesystems.
.TP
.BR \-\-level " \fIN\fR"
zstd compression level for file-name blocks (default 19).
.TP
.BR \-\-dict\-size " \fIBYTES\fR"
Maximum trained zstd dictionary size (default 65536; 0 disables).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Report progress for each build phase.
.SH DEFAULT INDEX
.B /var/lib/rlocate/rlocate.db
on Linux,
.B /var/db/rlocate/rlocate.db
on macOS when run as root; otherwise a per-user cache path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rlocate (1),
.BR updatedb (8)
